cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this atlas, please cite it as below, and cite the underlying studies listed on each study page."
title: "717 Atlas: a haplotype-resolved gene atlas for Populus tremula x alba clone INRA 717-1B4"
abstract: >-
  A static, browsable atlas of the 63,960 gene models in the two phased haplotypes of hybrid
  poplar clone 717, integrating GENESPACE synteny across a 12-genome panel, genEra
  phylostratigraphy, Phytozome v5.1 functional annotation, HAP1/HAP2 syntelog Ka/Ks, and a
  652-sample RNA-seq expression atlas drawn from 28 curated studies. Later releases add
  tandem-array and paralog duplication context, predicted protein disorder and
  ESMFold-derived secondary structure with mass-spectrometry peptide evidence, and 46,141
  reciprocal one-to-one orthologs to Populus trichocarpa derived from the same synteny run.
  Version 0.4.0 adopts an Idesia-corrected lineage-specific gene pool, replaces the peptide
  layer with a five-dataset re-search of public Populus mass spectra against a 717-inclusive
  database, adds Ka/Ks against Populus trichocarpa for 52,232 genes, and carries accessible-chromatin
  and histone-mark calls from GEO GSE128434 as a property of each gene's P. trichocarpa ortholog.
type: dataset
